BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 315 762 Td
(that no ships passed. The next morning,) Tj T*
(according to the harbour records, fishermen) Tj T*
(found the lantern room glass cracked in four) Tj T*
(places, yet the light had not gone out once) Tj T*
(during the night.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Today the tower is automated, and the) Tj T*
(ledgers rest in a climate-controlled archive) Tj T*
(beside navigation charts from the same) Tj T*
(decades. Researchers compare the two sources) Tj T*
(to estimate how shipping routes shifted as) Tj T*
(engines replaced sails. Their work depends) Tj T*
(on a simple practice repeated without fail:) Tj T*
(a person who wrote down what they saw, every) Tj T*
(single day, whether or not anything seemed) Tj T*
(to happen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Visitors who reach the top of the tower can) Tj T*
(still read a copy of the first entry, framed) Tj T*
(beside the lens. It notes a calm sea, a) Tj T*
(light westerly breeze, and three fishing) Tj T*
(boats returning late with full nets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 762 Td
(Every evening at dusk the keeper climbed the) Tj T*
(one hundred and twelve steps of the tower,) Tj T*
(wound the clockwork that turned the great) Tj T*
(lens, and wrote a single line in the ledger.) Tj T*
(Over forty years the ledger filled eleven) Tj T*
(volumes, and nearly every line recorded the) Tj T*
(same three facts: the time the lamp was lit,) Tj T*
(the direction of the wind, and the number of) Tj T*
(ships that passed before midnight.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Historians who later studied the ledgers) Tj T*
(found that the plain entries told a richer) Tj T*
(story than anyone expected. Long gaps) Tj T*
(between ships marked the winters when the) Tj T*
(northern harbour froze. A sudden rise in) Tj T*
(traffic matched the year a canal opened two) Tj T*
(hundred miles inland. Even the handwriting) Tj T*
(changed, growing smaller and more careful) Tj T*
(after the storm that destroyed the old pier.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The keeper never described the storm itself.) Tj T*
(The entry for that night reads only that the) Tj T*
(lamp was lit at seven minutes past five,) Tj T*
(that the wind blew from the south-west, and) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 790 Td
(The Lighthouse Keeper's Ledger) Tj T*
